      "side": 1,
      "message": "Despite the fact that another method does this (that method doesn\u0027t get called much I guess, since it is skipped for some situations), this can *crash spectacularly* if the path is not valid \"Modified UTF-8\".\n\nTry `ls -l /storage/emulated/0/test$\u0027u\\200b\u0027` and get a \"Software caused connection abort\" error and a big crash in logs. That `u\\200b` is from a typo I made. The backslash should come first, normally. Writing it this way instead is invalid enough to bring this issue to light.",
      "revId": "bf7a91241f86875f52387bd84bfb73bce005dd20",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
